    crm:P183i_has_representation <https://ids.lib.harvard.edu/ids/iiif/493309004/full/full/0/default.jpg> ;
    rdf:value """Friday, May 5, 1916, I Tatti
Sarnes and Cecil [Pinsent] 
Went over to the Bragiottis to hear Alice Garrett have a singing lesson. She has a good voice. M me  Bragiotti and her sister both sang - it was rather painful, such hideous voices. I fear Bragiotti’s system while it brings out the voice very well brings it out not sweet or delightful. Berry and I called on Aunt Janet, who came to dine, with Miss Hulton, who played. Bakst fell in love with her. """^^xsd:string ;
    mbdiaries-ontology:index 113 ;
    mbdiaries-ontology:part_of <https://mbdiaries.itatti.harvard.edu/resource/diary/1916> .

